   \[
   32 \text{ lb} \times \frac{1 \text{ kg}}{3.21 \text{ lb}} = 9.99 \text{ kg} \approx 10 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the total loading dose:**
   \[
   10 \text{ kg} \times 20 \text{ mg/kg} = 200 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time taken for infusion:**
   \[
   \frac{200 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 400 \text{ min}
   \]

