\[
\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightleftharpoons \text{HSO}_4^- + \text{H}^+
\]
The equilibrium for \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) with \( \text{M}^{2+} \) ions is:
\[
\text{H}_2\text{S} + \text{Mn}^{2+} \rightleftharpoons \text{MnS} + 2\text{H}^+
\]
The equilibrium constant for this reaction is:
\[
K_{sp} = [\text{H}^+]^2 [\text{MnS}]
\]
The solubility product \( K_{sp} \) of \( \text{MnS} \) is \( 1.8 \times 10^{-16} \). For \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \):
\[
\text{H}_2\text{S} + \text{Ni}^{2+} \rightleftharpoons \text{NiS} + 2\text{H}^+
\]
