1. Probability of getting 9 heads:
\[
\binom{12}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^9 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12-9} = \binom{12}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = \binom{12}{3} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 104 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
\]
2. Probability of getting 10 heads:
\[
