2H2(g) + O2(g) → 2H2O(l)

Now, we can calculate the standard Gibbs free energy change (ΔG°) for the reaction using the standard Gibbs free energy of formation (ΔG°f) for each species involved:

ΔG° = [2 × ΔG°f(H2O)] - [2 × ΔG°f(H2) + 1 × ΔG°f(O2)]

