- \( \mu_0 \) is the permeability of free space (\( 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T m/s} \)),
- \( I \) is the current (in Amerebs)
- \( r \) is the radius of the coil (in meters)

Given:
- Number of turns \( N = 100 \)
- Current \( I = 1 \, \text{A} \)
- Radius \( r = 0.2 \, \text{m} \)

The magnetic field strength at the center of the coil is:
\[
B = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times 1}{2\pi \times 0.2} = \frac{4 \times 10^{-7} \times 1}{2 \times 0.2} = \frac{4 \times 10^{-7}}{0.4} = 10 \times 10^{-7} = 10^{-6} \, \text{T}
\]
