   - **Particle Hardening (Preening):** The hard CuAl$_2 particles act as obstacles to dislocation movement. Dislocations will be trapped by these particles, requiring more stress to move through or through the path of the particles. This results in an increase in the yield strength. The higher the number of particles and the finer their size, the stronger the pinning effect and the higher the yield strength.
